    "q-110234": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110234",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "The following table gives the values of functions $f(x)$ and ${f}^{′}(x)$ at some points. Find $({f}^{-1})^{′}(4).$\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| $1$ | $4$ | $-2$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=4,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(4)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(4)=1$ and ${f}^{′}(1)=-2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(4) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
